# Lesson 3, new exercise: take your time at trick 1. Win in your hand and save dummy's ♠K as the way back to the clubs.
title: Save dummy's king
id: L03-10
type: exercise
lesson: 3
concepts: 3.5, 3.1, 3.2
student: S
board: 42
dealer: E
vulnerable: both

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  K32    873    54     KQJT8
  E  765    Q92    T987   943
  S  AQ4    AKJ5   AK63   72
  W  JT98   T64    QJ2    A65

auction:
  E Pass
  S 2NT*   = 21-22 points, balanced
     not *: 21 points and a balanced hand: what does the lesson open?
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = 4+ points: game
  E Pass
  S Pass
  W Pass

auction recap:
  You opened 2NT with 21 points, and partner raised to game. You are
  declarer, because you bid no-trump first, and so West will lead to the
  first trick.

planning:
  winners: 11
  spades: 3 = The ace, king and queen. Dummy's king is its only way in: save it.
  hearts: 2 = The ace and king.
  diamonds: 2 = The ace and king.
  clubs: 4 = Four, once the ace is gone, if you can reach them.
  remind: You need 9 tricks. Count the obvious winners in each suit.
  remind: Dummy's clubs can give four tricks once the ace is gone. How will you get to dummy to take them?
play:
  1   W SJ  N S2*  E S5  S SQ
      note: Seven winners on top: three spades, two hearts, two diamonds. Dummy's clubs can add four more once the ace is gone, but dummy has no other way in except the ♠K. So win this trick in your hand, and save the king.
      S2 key: Keep dummy's ♠K as a way to reach the clubs later. Your queen wins this trick.
      S2 not SK: Did you think about how you will reach dummy's clubs later? The ♠K is dummy's only way in.
  2   S C2  W C5  N CK  E C3
      note: Now force out the ♣A.
  3   N CQ  E C4  S C7  W CA
      note: Keep going until the ace is gone.
  4   W ST  N S3  E S6  S SA
      note: Win in your hand again. Dummy's ♠K is still waiting.
  5   S S4  W S8  N SK  E S7
      note: Now use the ♠K to reach dummy's clubs.
  6   N CJ  E C9  S D3  W C6
      note: Dummy's clubs are all winners.
  7   N CT  E D7  S D6  W D2
      note: Keep cashing dummy's clubs.
  8   N C8  E D8  S H5  W H4
      note: The last club.
  9   N H3  E H2  S HA  W H6
      note: Back to your hand for the red-suit winners.
  10  S HK  W HT  N H7  E H9
      note: The ♥K.
  11  S DA  W DJ  N D4  E D9
      note: Now the diamonds.
  12  S DK  W DQ  N D5  E DT
      note: The ♦K.
  13  S HJ  W S9  N H8  E HQ
      note: 11 tricks: 3NT made with two overtricks.

play recap:
  The plan: count seven winners on top, set up dummy's clubs, and keep the ♠K
  as the way to reach them.

  The decision that mattered came at trick 1. If dummy's king had won the
  first spade, the clubs would have been set up with no way to get to them.
